 Run `npm test` for simulation and progression checks. The simulation is deterministic for a given seed and input sequence and uses a fixed 60 Hz update with seconds-based timers.
 
+Release 1.0.1 was audited on 19 October 2026. See [AUDIT_REPORT.md](AUDIT_REPORT.md) for the detailed defect tracker, reproducible tests, browser evidence, CPU/heap measurements, and remaining verification limits. The regression suite now includes physics, navigation, client input, audio lifecycle, save protection, and actual standalone packaging checks.
+
+Run `npm run profile` for the repeatable 30-mission CPU/heap scenario. Run `npm run package` and then `npm run archive` to regenerate the HTML edition and verified source ZIP. Node 18+ is needed for development tools; Python 3 is used for the local server and source archive. Neither is needed to play the standalone file.
+
+Development browser diagnostics are available with `?audit=1`; they stay off during ordinary play and transmit no telemetry. Native fullscreen, physical touch/audio devices, graphics context loss, cross-browser behavior, and direct file-scheme opening have the verification limits documented in the audit report.
+
 ## Layout
 
 - `dist/sim.js`: movement, beam physics, entities, enemy behavior, encounter director, boss, scoring.
+- `dist/collision.js`: continuous AABB sweeps, overlap recovery, world contact and support queries.
 - `dist/render.js`: original procedural Canvas art, animation, effects, warnings.
 - `dist/app.js`: screens, campaign UI, input, fixed-step loop, results.
 - `dist/progression.js`: save validation, backups, purchases, reward calculation.
 - `dist/audio.js`: synthesized sound effects and tractor hum.
 - `dist/config.js`: mission and upgrade balance.
 - `tests/`: automated interaction and progression checks.
+- `audit/`: structured issue tracker, test evidence, profiles and browser screenshots.
 
 All game logic and artwork run locally. Web fonts are optional; system fallbacks work without a network. This is an original implementation rather than a literal port of archived ActionScript or assets. Monetization, advertising, platform stores, cloud saves, and online leaderboards are not included.
